msgid_plural "thermal electric balaclavas (on)"
msgstr[0] "발열 복면 (켜짐)"

#. ~ Description of "thermal electric balaclava (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"This is a snug cloth mask with internal battery-powered heating elements.  "
"It is are currently on, and continually draining batteries.  Use it to turn "
"it off."
msgstr ""
"배터리로 작동되는 발열장치가 내장된 포근한 면 재질의 발라클라바. 현재 작동 중이며 배터리를 소모하고 있습니다. 사용하면 전원이 "
"꺼집니다."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "pair of binoculars"
msgid_plural "pairs of binoculars"
msgstr[0] "쌍안경"

#. ~ Description of "pair of binoculars"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"A pair of optics with a neck strap attached.  Useful for seeing long "
"distances.  Wearing this item or carrying it in your inventory will double "
"the distance around you that is mapped during your travels.  You could also "
"use them to focus the sunlight."
msgstr ""
"목에 걸 수 있게 끈이 달린 광학장비로 먼 곳을 볼 때 유용합니다. 먼 거리를 볼 때 유용합니다. 물품을 착용하거나 인벤토리에 저장하면 "
"여행 중에 볼 수있는 주변 거리가 두 배로 늘어납니다.햇빛을 모을 때 쓸 수도 있습니다."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "headlamp"
msgid_plural "headlamps"
msgstr[0] "헤드램프"

#. ~ Description of "headlamp"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"This is an LED headlamp with an adjustable strap so as to be comfortably "
"worn on your head or attached to your helmet.  Use it to turn it on."
msgstr "머리에 쓰거나 헬멧에 달 수 있도록 조절할 수 있는 끈이 달린 LED 헤드 랜턴. 사용(a)하면 켜집니다."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "headlamp"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "You turn the headlamp on."
msgstr "헤드램프를 켭니다."

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "headlamp"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "The headlamp batteries are dead."
msgstr "헤드램프의 배터리가 나갔습니다."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "wearable camera"
msgid_plural "wearable cameras"
msgstr[0] "웨어러블 카메라"

#. ~ Description of "wearable camera"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"A point-and-shoot digital camera, with digital viewfinder, a backup 'iron-"
"sight', and flash.  You can look at your photos on the digital screen, or "
"transfer them with a memory card.  Takes conventional batteries.  This one "
"can be worn over your neck."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "wearable professional camera"
msgid_plural "wearable professional cameras"
msgstr[0] "웨어러블 전문가용 카메라"

#. ~ Description of "wearable professional camera"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"A 35mm digital SLR (single-lens reflex) camera, with optical and digital "
"viewfinders, zoom lens with auto-focus and stabilizer, and flash.  You can "
"view your photos on it or transfer them with a memory card; it runs on "
"conventional batteries.  Before the Cataclysm, you could have taken "
"professional-grade photos using this.  This one can be worn over your neck"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "headlamp (on)"
msgid_plural "headlamps (on)"
msgstr[0] "헤드램프 (켜짐)"

#. ~ Description of "headlamp (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"This is an LED headlamp with an adjustable strap so as to be comfortably "
"worn on your head or attached to your helmet.  It is turned on, and "
"continually draining batteries.  Use it to turn it off."
msgstr ""
"머리에 쓰거나 헬멧에 달 수 있도록 조절할 수 있는 끈이 달린 LED 헤드 랜턴. 현재 켜져있으며, 지속적으로 배터리를 소모하고 "
"있습니다. 사용(a)하면 꺼집니다."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "survivor headlamp"
msgid_plural "survivor headlamps"
msgstr[0] "생존용 헤드램프"

#. ~ Description of "survivor headlamp"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"This is a custom-made LED headlamp reinforced to be more durable, brighter, "
"and with a larger and more efficient battery pack.  The adjustable strap "
"allows it to be comfortably worn on your head or attached to your helmet.  "
"Use it to turn it on."
msgstr ""
"더 밝고 오래 가도록 크고 효율적인 배터리팩을 설치한 개조된 LED 헤드램프입니다. 머리에 쓰거나 헬멧에 달 수 있도록 조절할 수 있는 "
"끈이 달려있습니다. 사용하면 전원을 켭니다."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "survivor headlamp"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "You turn the survivor headlamp on."
msgstr "생존용 헤드램프를 켭니다."

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "survivor headlamp"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "The survivor headlamp batteries are dead."
msgstr "생존용 헤드랜턴의 배터리가 다 되었습니다."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "survivor headlamp (on)"
msgid_plural "survivor headlamps (on)"
msgstr[0] "생존용 헤드램프 (켜짐)"

#. ~ Description of "survivor headlamp (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"This is a custom-made LED headlamp reinforced to be more durable, brighter, "
"and with a larger and more efficient battery pack.  The adjustable strap "
"allows it to be comfortably worn on your head or attached to your helmet.  "
"It is turned on, and continually draining batteries.  Use it to turn it off."
msgstr ""
"더 밝고 오래 가도록 크고 효율적인 배터리팩을 설치한 개조된 LED 헤드램프입니다. 머리에 쓰거나 헬멧에 달 수 있도록 조절할 수 있는 "
"끈이 달려있습니다. 현재 켜져있으며 지속적으로 배터리를 소모하고 있습니다. 사용하면 전원을 끕니다."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid "atomic headlamp"
msgid_plural "atomic headlamps"
msgstr[0] "원자력 헤드램프"

#. ~ Description of "atomic headlamp"
#: data/json/items/tool_armor.json
msgid ""
"This is a custom-made reinforced headlamp powered by the magic of nuclear "
"decay, focused for more usable brightness.  The adjustable strap allows it "
"to be comfortably worn on your head or attached to your helmet.  Use it to "
"close the cover and hide the light."
msgstr ""
"핵에너지의 신비한 힘으로 돌아가는 개조된 강화 헤드램프입니다. 더 유용한 빛을 내는데 초점을 맞췄습니다. 머리에 쓰거나 헬멧에 달 수 "
"있도록 조절할 수 있는 끈이 달려있습니다. 사용하면 커버를 덮어 빛을 숨깁니다."

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "atomic headlamp"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "atomic lamp"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "atomic reading light"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "magical reading light"
#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json data/json/items/tool_armor.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/alchemy_items.json
